#!/usr/bin/python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
"""raye-tests -- the one launcher for every automated test suite of /srv/raye.

Until now nothing ran them. Each repository documents how its tests are
started (its README, its ctest wiring, the docstring of the file itself),
and that knowledge lived only there: a suite could rot for weeks without
anyone noticing, and two of them never ran in the mode that actually
proves something. This script holds that knowledge in one place, in
raye_tests_suites.py next to it, where every entry says where its own
command comes from.

    tools/raye-tests                     run everything runnable (default)
    tools/raye-tests list                what exists, how it runs, what it needs
    tools/raye-tests --repo iso          one repository
    tools/raye-tests --suite iso/purge   one suite (repeatable, glob allowed)
    tools/raye-tests --iso FILE          question that image (default: the newest)
    tools/raye-tests --no-iso            repository-only verdicts, no image
    tools/raye-tests --release           also the suites gated on RAYE_RELEASE
    tools/raye-tests --strict            a skip, or a cache left behind,
                                         fails the run too
    tools/raye-tests --json FILE         the same report, machine readable

Exit 0 when every suite that ran passed, 1 when one failed, 2 on a usage
error.

THE RULE THIS SCRIPT EXISTS FOR. A suite that cannot run is named, with
the reason, and never counted as a pass. A test skipped in silence is
worse than a test that does not exist, because the silence is read as
cover. Three concrete silences this launcher refuses:

  - "Ran 0 tests ... NO TESTS RAN" exits 0. Measured 2026-11-06 with
    python3 -m unittest discover on an empty folder. So a suite whose
    output can be counted must count at least one test, or it fails.
  - a test whose tool is missing can exit 0 after printing "skipped"
    (files/tests/raye/test_desktop_file.sh without desktop-file-validate),
    or exit 1 for want of a font (theme/tests/test_fonts.sh). Both look
    like a verdict and are not one. Their needs are declared here, so a
    missing tool makes a named skip, never a green and never a false red.
  - 77 is ctest's skip code and four tests of this tree already use it.
    It is honoured as a skip, with the test's own last line as the reason.

THIS SCRIPT WRITES NOTHING INTO THE REPOSITORIES. Every suite runs with
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, pytest without its cache, and work folders
under a temporary directory removed at the end. It does not build and it
does not package: a suite that needs a compiled tree is a named skip, so
the launcher can never take the machine away from an image build.
And it proves it rather than claiming it -- `git status --porcelain` of
every repository is fingerprinted before and after, and a change is
reported.

WHY IT LIVES IN THE iso REPOSITORY. /srv/raye is not itself a git
repository, so the launcher has to live inside one of the fourteen. iso
is the one that assembles the distribution and already carries tooling
that reaches across the others (tools/tests/test_publish_repo.py reads
../update/src). An umbrella repository would be a better home the day
one exists.
"""
